# Via Nova Design Standards

## Brand Fonts

- **Libre Baskerville**: Primary font for most text
- **Futura (and Futura Light)**: For small text, variety, and pacing of
  attention

## Brand Colors

- **Light Tint**: 100% or 80% of `#F7F7F7`
- **Dark Blue**: `#364153` (and percentages of)
- **Navy Blue**: `#202A2E`
- **Light Grey Blue**: `#677489`
- **Tint behind "Why Via"**: 15% of `#677489`

## Design Principles

1. Follow wireframe designs for desktop and mobile layouts including fonts,
   placement, and size
2. Ensure text animations are implemented as designed
3. Maintain consistent spacing between lines and text throughout
4. Use gradients on images - never go to fully clear on one side, always keep
   the lightest gradient at 15-20% of the overlay color
5. Ensure proper text alignment and prevent "type widows" (single words on a new
   line)

## Navigation

- Desktop: Navigation should be wider than content of main body
- Mobile: Use hamburger menu with consistent font treatment (no italics, same as
  desktop)
- Title safe area should be wider than Wix default to prevent text collisions
- Via Logo links to home page

## Images

- All images should be properly centered
- Use gradients overlays on images as specified
- Maintain consistent image quality and cropping

## Mobile Considerations

- Ensure mobile optimization is complete for all pages
- Hamburger menu items should be centered on mobile
- Text should properly rag (wrap) with correct alignment based on alphanumeric
  indicators
- Maintain consistent spacing above and below each line

## Interactive Elements

- Carousels should support swipe on mobile and cursor navigation on desktop
- Passive fade transitions should be implemented
- Hover states should be applied to interactive elements
- Sticky navigation should be used where appropriate

## Content Guidelines

- Maintain semantic HTML structure
- Use proper heading hierarchy
- Ensure accessibility with ARIA labels where needed
- Follow the approved text content from design notes
